  "known_limitations": [
    "Explicit C++17 translation of alexkazik/lzss 0.9.1 fixed EI10/EJ4/C32 profile. The original commit denotes reference provenance; current compiled inputs are the pinned C++ source closure. No Rust source, FFI, dependency or toolchain is used.",
    "282 streams frozen from the original implementation before removal match byte-for-byte, with live original cross-decode additionally recorded. Original-language upstream suites are retained as historical evidence, not executed by this C++ qualification.",
    "Only fixed benchmark parameters EI10/EJ4/C32, stack work buffers, one thread, one stream per routed object are registered; alternative profiles, streaming, query and random access remain unregistered.",
    "No checksum: structurally valid payload mutations require benchmark exactness validation. Strict decoder rejects truncated tokens, surplus bytes, length mismatch and nonzero padding before output mutation.",
    "C++ encoder, decoder, strict bitstream validator, ABI and native test runners use ASan/UBSan in sanitizer profile; system runtime is uninstrumented; LSan disabled for ptrace-based sandbox compatibility",
    "Current native and five-layer qualification do not relabel pre-migration formal performance or frozen V3.2 acceptance as C++ results; new experiments require new current implementation identities.",
    "block_size is a framework boundary fixture parameter, not a second LZSS window or an implicit segmentation stage.",
    "Local lzbench has LZSSE2/4/8, not this specified Okumura EI10/EJ4 format; source exception remains explicit."
  ],
